# Simulated runs (`forge script` without --broadcast) write here. The addresses come
# from a simulated sender, so the file is never a deployment record; only the
# broadcast's ./deployments/<chainId>.json is. See script/Deploy.s.sol:deploymentFile.
*.dry-run.json

# Local-node runs (`anvil --fork-url ... --chain-id 143` plus `--broadcast`). The chain id
# is mainnet's and the broadcast is real, so only `localFork` separates these addresses
# from the ones on Monad. See script/Deploy.s.sol:isLocalFork.
*.local.json

# Broadcasts that have not been confirmed on chain. forge writes files while it executes
# the script, before it sends anything, so these name addresses that may never have got
# code. `--sig "confirm()"` checks them and writes the real record. See
# script/DeployClaims.s.sol.
*.pending.json
